p-adic tree = channels (level 1) + coupling (deeper) + apex (residue 0) (oracle-S542)

=== n=12: channels mod n/2=6; channel prime p=3; factor n=12=2^2*3^1 ===
  LEVEL-1 (mod 3) nodes = 3 channels:
     residue 0: [3, 6, 9]  <- APEX / gate channel (residue 0; the speed n/2 family)
     residue 1: [1, 4, 7, 10]
     residue 2: [2, 5, 8, 11]
  COUPLING: 3/3 level-1 nodes split further at level 2 (mod 9)
  endpoint MOAT depth (S410) d_p = v_p(n): {2: 2, 3: 1}
  apex speed n/2 = 6: residue mod 3 = 0 (=0 means apex is the gate channel)

=== n=14: channels mod n/2=7; channel prime p=7; factor n=14=2^1*7^1 ===
  LEVEL-1 (mod 7) nodes = 7 channels:
     residue 0: [7]  <- APEX / gate channel (residue 0; the speed n/2 family)
     residue 1: [1, 8]
     residue 2: [2, 9]
     residue 3: [3, 10]
     residue 4: [4, 11]
     residue 5: [5, 12]
     residue 6: [6, 13]
  COUPLING: 6/7 level-1 nodes split further at level 2 (mod 49)
  endpoint MOAT depth (S410) d_p = v_p(n): {2: 1, 7: 1}
  apex speed n/2 = 7: residue mod 7 = 0 (=0 means apex is the gate channel)

=== n=16: channels mod n/2=8; channel prime p=2; factor n=16=2^4 ===
  LEVEL-1 (mod 2) nodes = 2 channels:
     residue 0: [2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14]  <- APEX / gate channel (residue 0; the speed n/2 family)
     residue 1: [1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15]
  COUPLING: 2/2 level-1 nodes split further at level 2 (mod 4)
  endpoint MOAT depth (S410) d_p = v_p(n): {2: 4}
  apex speed n/2 = 8: residue mod 2 = 0 (=0 means apex is the gate channel)

=== n=18: channels mod n/2=9; channel prime p=3; factor n=18=2^1*3^2 ===
  LEVEL-1 (mod 3) nodes = 3 channels:
     residue 0: [3, 6, 9, 12, 15]  <- APEX / gate channel (residue 0; the speed n/2 family)
     residue 1: [1, 4, 7, 10, 13, 16]
     residue 2: [2, 5, 8, 11, 14, 17]
  COUPLING: 3/3 level-1 nodes split further at level 2 (mod 9)
  endpoint MOAT depth (S410) d_p = v_p(n): {2: 1, 3: 2}
  apex speed n/2 = 9: residue mod 3 = 0 (=0 means apex is the gate channel)

READING: the p-adic tree is the common object. Level 1 = the S532 CHANNELS
(= floor(n/2) = the independent-pair matching); the residue-0 branch = the APEX
/ source-sink / speed n/2 (S530, S541's diameter pair). The CHANNEL COUPLING
(why n>=6 is multi-channel, S531/S532) = the tree DEPTH (level-2+ refinement).
The endpoint MOAT (S410) = the boundary at depth v_p(n). The annular-braid CENTER
= shift (S541) = translation toward the tree boundary, so LRC is a boundary
condition. Covering character sums (S526) = harmonic analysis on this tree.
